{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 36}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   This draft describes the general problem of encryption of the Server\n   Name Identification (SNI) parameter.  The proposed solutions hide a\n   Hidden Service behind a Fronting Service, only disclosing the SNI of\n   the Fronting Service to external observers.  The draft lists known\n   attacks against SNI encryption, discusses the current \"co-tenancy\n   fronting\" solution, and presents requirements for future TLS layer\n   solutions.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption/", "expires": "2018-11-21T20:10:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 230534, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>, Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/230534/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2018-11-19T00:03:52Z", "title": "Issues and Requirements for SNI Encryption in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This draft describes the general problem of encryption of the Server\n   Name Identification (SNI) parameter.  The proposed solutions hide a\n   Hidden Service behind a Fronting Service, only disclosing the SNI of\n   the Fronting Service to external observers.  The draft lists known\n   attacks against SNI encryption, discusses the current \"co-tenancy\n   fronting\" solution, and presents requirements for future TLS layer\n   solutions.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption/", "expires": "2018-11-21T20:10:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 230531, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/230531/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2018-11-18T23:29:03Z", "title": "Issues and Requirements for SNI Encryption in TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This draft describes the general problem of encryption of the Server\n   Name Identification (SNI) parameter.  The proposed solutions hide a\n   Hidden Service behind a Fronting Service, only disclosing the SNI of\n   the Fronting Service to external observers.  The draft starts by\n   listing known attacks against SNI encryption, discusses the current\n   \"co-tenancy fronting\" solution, and then presents two potential TLS\n   layer solutions that might mitigate these attacks.\n   The first solution is based on TLS in TLS \"quasi tunneling\", and the\n   second solution is based on \"combined tickets\".  These solutions only\n   require minimal extensions to the TLS protocol.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption/", "expires": "2018-03-03T06:36:23Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 199639, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/199639/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2017-08-30T05:36:23Z", "title": "SNI Encryption in TLS Through Tunneling", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This draft describes the general problem of encryption of the Server\n   Name Identification (SNI) parameter.  The proposed solutions hide a\n   Hidden Service behind a Fronting Service, only disclosing the SNI of\n   the Fronting Service to external observers.  The draft starts by\n   listing known attacks against SNI encryption, discusses the current\n   \"co-tenancy fronting\" solution, and then presents two potential TLS\n   layer solutions that might mitigate these attacks.\n   The first solution is based on TLS in TLS \"quasi tunneling\", and the\n   second solution is based on \"combined tickets\".  These solutions only\n   require minimal extensions to the TLS protocol.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption/", "expires": "2018-09-02T23:28:12Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 210850, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/210850/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2018-03-02T00:28:12Z", "title": "SNI Encryption in TLS Through Tunneling", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This draft describes the general problem of encryption of the Server\n   Name Identification (SNI) parameter.  The proposed solutions hide a\n   Hidden Service behind a Fronting Service, only disclosing the SNI of\n   the Fronting Service to external observers.  The draft starts by\n   listing known attacks against SNI encryption, discusses the current\n   \"co-tenancy fronting\" solution, and then presents two potential TLS\n   layer solutions that might mitigate these attacks.\n   The first solution is based on TLS in TLS \"quasi tunneling\", and the\n   second solution is based on \"combined tickets\".  These solutions only\n   require minimal extensions to the TLS protocol.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption/", "expires": "2018-08-23T19:01:15Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 210064, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 22, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/210064/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2018-02-19T20:01:15Z", "title": "SNI Encryption in TLS Through Tunneling", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This draft describes the general problem of encryption of the Server\n   Name Identification (SNI) parameter.  The proposed solutions hide a\n   Hidden Service behind a Fronting Service, only disclosing the SNI of\n   the Fronting Service to external observers.  The draft lists known\n   attacks against SNI encryption, discusses the current \"co-tenancy\n   fronting\" solution, and presents requirements for future TLS layer\n   solutions.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption/", "expires": "2018-11-21T20:10:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 218211, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-sni-encryption", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/218211/", "rev": "03", "rfc_nu